{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1498789-playing-path-of-death-and-the-soul","id":1498789,"title":"Playing Path of Death and the Soul","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-12-04T13:00:15-08:00","id":1498789,"title":"Playing Path of Death and the Soul","content":"Hello everyone. So, I'm attempting to challenge myself by playing a Path character and I have chosen Death and the Soul for a Malkavian antitribu I'm making. This path has appealed to me quite a lot due to its academic and mystical nature and with its focus on the soul and emotions (as well as managing them and not being overcome by them), the hereafter and the future, and what comes after it all.<br /> <br /> However. Reading the hierarchy of sins for this particular Path makes it feel as though it was not designed for actual play. Yes, I know Paths are supposed to be inhuman philosophies and religions, but there are times when it feels as though they are trying <i>too hard</i> to be monstrous. This Path is populated by academics, cold and &quot;callous&quot;, but some of its sins do not seem to support that. I suppose I may not be verbalizing what I think about this Path perfectly, but let me expand upon it <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table_article-table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_article-table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\"> &quot;</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">Preventing a Death.</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">All things must die. Don't meddle with the universe's cycle.&quot;</td> </tr> </table></div> This is, perhaps, one of the most painful sins to work with. Does this mean I have to let an ally die while we are in a conflict just &quot;because&quot;? Am I to observe their death spasms amidst a hail of blades, fire, and nasty words? How does one rationalize this, especially to thinking, immortal creatures?<br /> <br /> I must stress that I genuinely want to play a character on this Path and I understand they're meant to be inhuman, but the rationale and sins themselves make such characters beyond difficult.<br /> <br /> For anyone who <i>has</i> played a character on this Path, how did you do it and how did it go? Did you change the sins? Ignore them? Play it to the letter? Interpret each sin according to your character?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2204-toreador","name":"Toreador","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2204_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-04T14:44:42-08:00","id":1498801,"title":"","content":"&quot;Preventing a Death&quot; isn't that hard... vampires don't exactly have a bunch of healing magic to use to do anything about someone that's dying.<br /> <br /> Yes, that does mean if one of your allies is mortally wounded, you have to let them die, and sit there and watch it happen. The Path is about studying death, and not fearing it.<br /> <br /> In play, Death and the Soul PCs are generally just not expected to be reliable in combat. Combat is anathema to their desire to act on rational lines of thought instead of emotions and instincts. Killing an opponent and not taking time to observer their death even with fighting happening all around is a difficultly easily avoided by just not participating in the fight in the first place and using Disciplines to observe without interfering.<br /> <br /> If you're in a game where Path vampires are playable options, it means your in a larger social structure where that's going to be accounted for. The pre-V5 Sabbat have explicit difficult dynamics juggling the needs of Path vampires with the needs of Sect leadership, but respecting Path needs is important to keeping the Sect functional so they find ways to compromise. Institutionally, the Sabbat knows what Death and the Soul is about, and know what to expect out of its followers. If you send one to assassinate someone, you know to factor in that they're going to want to take their time, not get in, kill, and get out ASAP. They're not front line fighters for the Sect. Other Cainites can handle that. Path vampires don't have to explain themselves to Path-diverse groups because everyone is following their own way the best they can and want everyone else to participate in mutual respect of those choices.<br /> <br /> -------------<br /> <br /> That all said: Path sins are meant to be committed. They're no there just to be flavor. Your PC might slavishly to their best to abide by every tenet and precept of their Path, but you as the player (even for Humanity!) should be expecting stories where that's no possible. Your PC's dedication will be challenged. They will be put in situations where there is no good answer, just picking the least worst answer from their limited perspective. The whole point is the narrative drama of seeing what happens when characters get put into difficult situations. Paths just create a very specific set of difficulties that other characters don't face (while frequently not dealing with difficulties other characters do face in the exchange).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}